v11.0 established that recoverability gives an atemporal partial order but does not select one
actual strict descent.

v11.1 asks what the weakest new physical datum is that can select such a descent without
introducing time, entropy, geometry, or an arbitrary CPTP map.

The answer is a retained observable algebra.

We call the primitive:

\[
\boxed{
\textbf{Retained Algebra Selection (RAS)}
}
\]

A pruning event specifies a proper unital observable subalgebra

\[
\boxed{
\mathcal R_{\rm next}
\subsetneq
\mathcal R_{\rm current}
}
\]

whose observables remain recoverable.

Once \(\mathcal R_{\rm next}\) is selected, the pruning map itself is not another free object.

In finite-dimensional tracial quantum theory it is the unique trace-preserving conditional
expectation

\[
\boxed{
E_{\mathcal R_{\rm next}}
:
\mathcal R_{\rm current}
\rightarrow
\mathcal R_{\rm next}.
}
\]

Thus the irreducible physical choice is the retained algebra, not an arbitrary channel.

This closes the minimal **nonselective** pruning primitive conditionally on accepting RAS.

It does not yet select one measurement outcome or branch.

\[
\boxed{
\textbf{RCR: choose one nonzero central record projection }z\in Z(\mathcal R)
}
\]

as actual.

For a fully resolved classical event, take \(z\) minimal central.

The selective state is

\[
\boxed{
\rho_z
=
\frac{
zE_\mathcal R(\rho)z
}{
\operatorname{Tr}[zE_\mathcal R(\rho)]
}.
}
\]

RAS supplies:

- \(\mathcal R\);
- its center;
- the set of central alternatives.

RCR adds only:

\[
\boxed{
\textbf{actuality of one alternative.}
}
\]

It does not add:

- a clock;
- entropy;
- a new basis;
- an arbitrary instrument;
- geometry;
- or a change to pre-time gravity.

# UQCF–GEM v11.3 — Ordinal Event Time / Reparameterization Gate

## Adjudication

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{ORDINAL\ EVENT\ TIME:\ DERIVED\ CONDITIONAL\ ON\ RAS+RCR}
}
\]

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{GLOBAL\ EVENT\ ORDER:\ PARTIAL,\ NOT\ TOTAL}
}
\]

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{METRIC/CLOCK\ TIME:\ NOT\ DERIVED}
}
\]

v11.2 established that RAS supplies possible classical records through the center of the retained
algebra, while RCR supplies actuality of one record.

Once actual records refine one another,

\[
z_{k+1}\le z_k,
\]

the realized history acquires an intrinsic order.

v11.3 asks whether that order justifies an emergent notion of time.

The answer is:

\[
\boxed{
\textbf{yes for ordinal event time, no for metric/clock time.}
}
\]

A finite realized branch has an intrinsic order type and therefore an intrinsic ordinal event
position.

However, every strictly increasing real-valued labeling of that chain represents the same event
order. The theory does not select interval lengths, duration ratios, clock rate, or global
simultaneity.

No entropy, geometry, or external time coordinate is assumed.

---

# UQCF–GEM v11.4 — Intrinsic Duration / Clock-Candidate Gate

## Adjudication

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{ORDINAL\ TIME:\ RETAINED}
}
\]

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{WELL\!-\!BEHAVED\ STATE\!-\!INDEPENDENT\ DURATION\ FUNCTIONALS:\ EXIST}
}
\]

but

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{UNIQUE\ METRIC\ DURATION:\ NOT\ DERIVED}
}
\]

and more strongly,

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{THE\ REMAINING\ FREEDOM\ IS\ NOT\ MERELY\ CLOCK\ UNITS.}
}
\]

v11.3 established an intrinsic ordinal event time, conditional on RAS + RCR.

v11.4 asks whether the retained-algebra / recoverability structure also selects a scalar measure
of **how much** pruning occurred, strong enough to function as physical duration.

The answer is negative.

There is an infinite family of state-independent pruning intervals satisfying all of the
structural requirements tested here:

- positivity on every strict retained-algebra inclusion;
- additivity under nested pruning;
- additivity under independent tensor-product pruning;
- covariance / algebra-isomorphism invariance;
- spectator neutrality.

These candidates remain inequivalent even after fixing one common clock unit.

Therefore metric duration is underdetermined by the current pruning architecture.

No entropy, geometry, or background time is assumed.

# UQCF–GEM v11.5 — Clock-Selection Primitive / Dynamics Coupling Gate

## Adjudication

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{P2\ IS\ MATHEMATICALLY\ PRIVILEGED\ BY\ THE\ ACTUAL\ REVERSIBLE\ MOTION\ SPACE}
}
\]

but

\[
\boxed{
\texttt{P2\ IS\ NOT\ DERIVED\ FROM\ FROZEN\ DYNAMICS\ ALONE}
}
\]

The missing bridge is isolated as:

\[
\boxed{
\textbf{Motion-Capacity Clock Calibration (MCCC)}
}
\]

with

\[
\boxed{
\Delta\tau
=
\kappa
\log
\frac{
\dim_{\mathbb R}\mathfrak u(\mathcal R_{\rm before})
}{
\dim_{\mathbb R}\mathfrak u(\mathcal R_{\rm after})
}
=
\kappa D_2.
}
\]

Under MCCC, \(p=2\) is selected and only one overall unit scale \(\kappa>0\) remains.

However, MCCC is a new physical bridge. It is not already implied by the frozen pre-time motion law.

Therefore metric time remains **conditional** rather than derived unconditionally.

No entropy, geometry, or background clock is introduced.
